  "raw_response": "{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/5383754233\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317#issuecomment-5383754233\",\"issue_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317\",\"id\":5383754233,\"node_id\":\"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABQOWR-Q\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"realmarcin\",\"id\":4625870,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?u=4a54630ef210e4f76a452eea65cda1b56370734c&v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/realmarcin\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"created_at\":\"2026-08-23T02:15:08Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-23T02:15:08Z\",\"author_association\":\"MEMBER\",\"body\":\"**Re-measured 2026-08-22 against `main`. The numbers here are stale rather than wrong — most of this shipped.**\\n\\n`scripts/regrade_synonym_matches.py` landed with **157 re-grades applied** in #325. Reproducing this issue's own stated method from scratch now finds ~142 more candidates, which reconciles with the original 297 (297 − 157 ≈ 140). But the committed script — which additionally skips records whose only evidence is *circular* — reports **25** remaining:\\n\\n```\\nnot_exact_match          903\\nnot_chebi                163\\nlabel_matches           1335\\nno_chebi_synonym_match    49\\ncircular_evidence_only    90\\ndeeper_defect_skipped      1\\nregrade                   25\\n```\\n\\nSo the re-grade half is **25 records from done**, not 297.\\n\\n## The residual is 235, not 59 — and it is five different problems\\n\\nThe \\\"matches nothing in ChEBI\\\" set is far larger than this issue estimated. Categorised:\\n\\n| n | disposition | example |\\n|---:|---|---|\\n| 90 | trivial-vs-systematic naming | `2-Piperidinone` → `piperidin-2-one` |\\n| 61 | **formula-as-label** | `Alcl3_X_6_H2o` → `aluminium trichloride hexahydrate` |\\n| 40 | scope loss (record has a qualifier the term lacks) | `Acetate_Carbon_Source` → `acetate` |\\n| 38 | qualified name (salt / solution / from-X) | `05_M_Nitrilotriacetic_Acid_Disodium_Salt` → `sodium nitrilotriacetate` |\\n| 6 | term more specific than the record | `Alanosine` → `L-alanosine`; `D` → `sodium lactate` (plainly wrong) |\\n\\nTwo things follow:\\n\\n- The **61 formula-as-label** are the `capitalize()` scars (#147 / #443) and overlap the hydrate family (#321, #334). They can never match a ChEBI string because the \\\"name\\\" is a formula, so no synonym-based rule will ever clear them — they want doing **with** the hydrate work, not here.\\n- The target grade differs per class, so this is not one mechanical pass. `SYNONYM_MATCH` is wrong for all five (no synonym exists); the naming classes want `LEXICAL_MATCH`, the scope-loss ones want `NARROW_MATCH` or `CLOSE_MATCH`.\\n\\n## One more correction\\n\\nOf the synonym-justified matches, **every one rests on `oio:hasRelatedSynonym`; none on `hasExactSynonym`**. Spot-checked and they do look like genuine identity (`2-mercaptoethanesulfonate` → `CHEBI:17905` coenzyme M; `2-chloro-4-ethylamino-6-isopropylamino-1,3,5-triazine` → `CHEBI:15930` atrazine), but it is a weaker justification than this issue implies and worth stating.\\n\\nNote for anyone reproducing: semsql stores subjects as **CURIEs**, not IRIs. Querying `statements` by IRI returns nothing, which reads exactly like \\\"this term has no synonyms\\\" — it silently produced a 0/377 split before I caught it.\",\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/5383754233/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"minimized\":null,\"pin\":null}",
